# SLED PUSH

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Sled Push is a whole-body locomotion exercise performed by driving a weighted sled across the ground.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the most effective exercises for developing horizontal force production, acceleration mechanics and work capacity while minimizing eccentric loading.

---

# Philosophy

The Sled Push teaches athletes to apply force directly into the ground.

Unlike most strength exercises, almost all muscular work is concentric.

This allows athletes to generate high levels of force while recovering rapidly.

CAS frequently selects the Sled Push during phases emphasizing power, acceleration or conditioning.

